<title>RUSSIA: Russian non-CIS Jan-April oil exports rise yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Russian non-CIS Jan-April oil exports rise yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian oil exports in January-April outside the Commonwealth of Independent States, or CIS, rose 9.9 percent year-on-year to 34.07 million tonnes (2.04 million barrels per day), Fuel and Energy Ministry data showed.</p>
<p>A report from the ministry's commercial information service InfoTEK said total crude exports, including to CIS countries, were up 3.8 percent in the first four months of 1997 to 40.48 million tonnes (2.43 million bpd).</p>
<p>The Black Sea port of Novorossiisk continued to dominate exports, accounting for 25 percent of total deliveries in the first four months.</p>
